[L:1] +# Quantum — Autonomous Trading Intelligence Platform
[L:2] +## Architecture, UI & Build Specification v2.0
[L:3] +
[L:4] +---
[L:5] +
[L:6] +> *Critical Update: Quantum is not a manual trading terminal. It is a fully autonomous trading intelligence system that analyzes markets, makes decisions, and executes paper trades without human intervention. The user is an overseer, not an operator. The system trades while you sleep, while you work, while you are with your kid. Your job is to configure it, monitor it, and trust it — because you built it to be trustworthy.*
[L:7] +
[L:8] +---
[L:9] +
[L:10] +## 1. The Autonomous Philosophy
[L:11] +
[L:12] +### 1.1 What "Autonomous" Means
[L:13] +
[L:14] +Quantum does not suggest trades. It **takes** trades. The full pipeline runs automatically:
[L:15] +
[L:16] +```
[L:17] +Market Data Arrives
[L:18] +    ↓
[L:19] +Data Quality Validated Automatically
[L:20] +    ↓
[L:21] +All Engines Run Automatically
[L:22] +    ↓
[L:23] +Master Decision Engine Decides Automatically
[L:24] +    ↓
[L:25] +Risk Gate Validates Automatically
[L:26] +    ↓
[L:27] +Portfolio Gate Validates Automatically
[L:28] +    ↓
[L:29] +Paper Order Created Automatically
[L:30] +    ↓
[L:31] +Simulated Fill Executed Automatically
[L:32] +    ↓
[L:33] +Position Monitored Automatically (SL/TP/Trailing)
[L:34] +    ↓
[L:35] +Position Closed Automatically
[L:36] +    ↓
[L:37] +Trade Review Generated Automatically
[L:38] +    ↓
[L:39] +Knowledge Updated Automatically
[L:40] +    ↓
[L:41] +Alert Sent to User if Significant Event
[L:42] +```
[L:43] +
[L:44] +**The human is not in the execution loop.** The human sets the guardrails, monitors the dashboard, and intervenes only when the system asks for help or when something goes wrong.
[L:45] +
[L:46] +### 1.2 Why Autonomous?
[L:47] +
[L:48] +Because the mistakes that cost me thousands happened when **I** was at the keyboard:
[L:49] +- I hesitated on a valid setup and missed the entry
[L:50] +- I overrode the system because "this time is different"
[L:51] +- I revenge-traded after a loss
[L:52] +- I moved my stop because I couldn't accept the loss
[L:53] +- I took a setup outside kill zones because I was bored
[L:54] +- I ignored the higher timeframe because the lower timeframe looked "so good"
[L:55] +- I traded while emotional, while tired, while distracted by my kid
[L:56] +
[L:57] +**The system does not get emotional. The system does not get tired. The system does not get FOMO. The system follows the rules.**
[L:58] +
[L:59] +### 1.3 The Human Role: Overseer, Not Operator
[L:60] +
[L:61] +| Operator (Old Way) | Overseer (Quantum Way) |
[L:62] +|---|---|
[L:63] +| Watches charts all day | Checks dashboard when convenient |
[L:64] +| Manually clicks "Buy" | Reviews what the system did |
[L:65] +| Decides position size | Configured risk profile once |
[L:66] +| Moves stop loss manually | Trusts the system's stop placement |
[L:67] +| Revenge trades after loss | System pauses automatically, sends alert |
[L:68] +| Trades outside kill zones | System only trades during configured windows |
[L:69] +| Forgets to review losses | System generates review automatically |
[L:70] +| Sizes on confidence | System sizes on math |
[L:71] +| Emotional decision-making | Evidence-based, rule-based execution |
[L:72] +
[L:73] +**The user configures, monitors, reviews, and intervenes. The system executes.**
[L:74] +
[L:75] +---
[L:76] +
[L:77] +## 2. System Architecture — Autonomous Mode
[L:78] +
[L:79] +### 2.1 High-Level Design
[L:80] +
[L:81] +```
[L:82] +┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
