[L:388] +## 4. The Command Center UI
[L:389] +
[L:390] +### 4.1 Design Philosophy
[L:391] +
[L:392] +The UI is a **mission control center**, not a trading terminal. Think:
[L:393] +- **NASA Mission Control** — Operators monitor systems, they don't fly the rocket
[L:394] +- **Datadog Dashboard** — Metrics, alerts, health, all real-time
[L:395] +- **Bloomberg Terminal** — Dense information, professional, no fluff
[L:396] +
[L:397] +**Key principles:**
[L:398] +- **Density over whitespace** — Every pixel shows useful data
[L:399] +- **Color is semantic** — Green = good/profit, Red = bad/loss, Yellow = warning, Blue = information
[L:400] +- **Alerts are prominent** — Critical events demand attention
[L:401] +- **History is accessible** — Every decision, every trade, every alert is logged and searchable
[L:402] +- **Configuration is powerful** — The user has fine-grained control over what the system does
[L:403] +
