[L:600] +# 16. Machine Learning System
[L:601] +
[L:602] +The ML system is one of the major components of Quantum.
[L:603] +
[L:604] +There are two major implementations.
[L:605] +
[L:606] +## TensorFlow.js
[L:607] +
[L:608] +The project defines three model architectures.
[L:609] +
[L:610] +### Dense Model
[L:611] +
[L:612] +A feed-forward neural network for tabular features.
[L:613] +
[L:614] +``` text
[L:615] +Features
[L:616] +   ↓
[L:617] +Dense
[L:618] +   ↓
[L:619] +Dropout
[L:620] +   ↓
[L:621] +Dense
[L:622] +   ↓
[L:623] +Output
[L:624] +```
[L:625] +
[L:626] +### LSTM Model
[L:627] +
[L:628] +Designed for sequential/time-series data.
[L:629] +
[L:630] +``` text
[L:631] +Candle Sequence
[L:632] +      ↓
[L:633] +     LSTM
[L:634] +      ↓
[L:635] +     LSTM
[L:636] +      ↓
[L:637] +    Dense
[L:638] +      ↓
[L:639] + Prediction
[L:640] +```
[L:641] +
[L:642] +### Transformer-Inspired Model
[L:643] +
[L:644] +The current implementation is a lightweight attention-inspired
[L:645] +architecture.
[L:646] +
[L:647] +It uses:
[L:648] +
[L:649] +-   Dense projection
[L:650] +-   Attention-like weighting
[L:651] +-   Global average pooling
[L:652] +-   Feed-forward layers
[L:653] +-   Classification/regression output
[L:654] +
[L:655] +This should be described as **transformer-inspired**, not a full
[L:656] +production Transformer architecture.
[L:657] +
