[L:821] +
[L:822] +# 21. Evidence-Based Decision Making
[L:823] +
[L:824] +The Master Decision Engine does not simply ask:
[L:825] +
[L:826] +``` text
[L:827] +Is RSI oversold?
[L:828] +```
[L:829] +
[L:830] +Instead, it collects evidence.
[L:831] +
[L:832] +Each evidence item can contain concepts such as:
[L:833] +
[L:834] +``` text
[L:835] +engineName
[L:836] +direction
[L:837] +confidence
[L:838] +weight
[L:839] +description
[L:840] +```
[L:841] +
[L:842] +Directions include:
[L:843] +
[L:844] +``` text
[L:845] +bullish
[L:846] +bearish
[L:847] +neutral
[L:848] +```
[L:849] +
[L:850] +The system then combines evidence from multiple engines.
[L:851] +
[L:852] +------------------------------------------------------------------------
[L:853] +
[L:854] +# 22. Contradiction Detection
[L:855] +
[L:856] +Quantum explicitly attempts to identify conflicting evidence.
[L:857] +
[L:858] +Example:
[L:859] +
[L:860] +``` text
[L:861] +Structure Engine → Bullish
[L:862] +Indicator Engine → Bearish
[L:863] +```
[L:864] +
[L:865] +The system can classify this as a contradiction.
[L:866] +
[L:867] +Contradictions reduce the final confidence score.
[L:868] +
[L:869] +This is important because a professional decision system should not hide
[L:870] +disagreement between analytical models.
[L:871] +
[L:872] +------------------------------------------------------------------------
[L:873] +
[L:874] +# 23. Confidence Engine
[L:875] +
[L:876] +The confidence calculation considers factors such as:
[L:877] +
[L:878] +-   Evidence quality
[L:879] +-   Evidence agreement
[L:880] +-   Evidence independence
[L:881] +-   Historical sample quality
[L:882] +-   Model calibration
[L:883] +-   Regime stability
[L:884] +-   Data freshness
[L:885] +-   Risk conditions
[L:886] +-   Contradiction penalties
[L:887] +
[L:888] +The resulting confidence is bounded between:
[L:889] +
[L:890] +``` text
[L:891] +0 and 1
[L:892] +```
[L:893] +
[L:894] +------------------------------------------------------------------------
[L:895] +
