[L:1009] +
[L:1010] +# 29. Walk-Forward Testing
[L:1011] +
[L:1012] +The current implementation includes walk-forward testing.
[L:1013] +
[L:1014] +The data is divided into:
[L:1015] +
[L:1016] +``` text
[L:1017] +70% → In-Sample
[L:1018] +30% → Out-of-Sample
[L:1019] +```
[L:1020] +
[L:1021] +The system compares performance to determine whether a strategy's
[L:1022] +historical performance persists outside the initial sample.
[L:1023] +
[L:1024] +------------------------------------------------------------------------
[L:1025] +
[L:1026] +# 30. Monte Carlo Simulation
[L:1027] +
[L:1028] +The backtesting suite also includes Monte Carlo simulation.
[L:1029] +
[L:1030] +The objective is to resample trade sequences to estimate possible
[L:1031] +distributions of:
[L:1032] +
[L:1033] +-   Returns
[L:1034] +-   Drawdowns
[L:1035] +-   Performance variability
[L:1036] +
[L:1037] +This helps evaluate whether a strategy's historical result may be
[L:1038] +dependent on a particular sequence of trades.
