[L:371] +## 7. Paper Trading — The Simulation
[L:372] +
[L:373] +### 7.1 The Execution Flow
[L:374] +
[L:375] +```
[L:376] +Decision: BUY
[L:377] +    ↓
[L:378] +User clicks "Execute Paper Trade"
[L:379] +    ↓
[L:380] +System creates Paper Order
[L:381] +    ↓
[L:382] +Simulated Fill (next candle open or current close + slippage)
[L:383] +    ↓
[L:384] +Position Opened
[L:385] +    ↓
[L:386] +Live P&L tracking on chart (unrealized P&L line)
[L:387] +    ↓
[L:388] +Stop Loss monitored every candle
[L:389] +    ↓
[L:390] +Take Profit 1 monitored — if hit, partial close (e.g., 50% of position)
[L:391] +    ↓
[L:392] +Take Profit 2 monitored — if hit, partial close (e.g., 30% of position)
[L:393] +    ↓
[L:394] +Take Profit 3 monitored — if hit, close remainder (20%)
[L:395] +    ↓
[L:396] +If Stop Loss hit → Position Closed, loss recorded
[L:397] +    ↓
[L:398] +Trade Review automatically generated
[L:399] +```
[L:400] +
[L:401] +### 7.2 Slippage and Fees
[L:402] +- **Slippage**: Random 0-2 pips on entry/exit, based on ATR and session (wider in Asian, tighter in London/NY)
[L:403] +- **Commission**: 0.1% per side (configurable by asset class)
[L:404] +- **Spread**: Simulated based on session and volatility (1-3 pips for majors, 5-10 pips for exotics)
[L:405] +
[L:406] +### 7.3 Position Visualization
[L:407] +- Open positions are shown on the chart with a **position line** — a horizontal line at entry price, colored green (profitable) or red (losing)
[L:408] +- Stop loss is a red line below/above entry
[L:409] +- Take profits are green dashed lines
[L:410] +- As price moves, the **unrealized P&L** is shown in real-time on the position line
[L:411] +- When a target is hit, a **fill marker** appears on the chart with the partial close details
[L:412] +
[L:413] +### 7.4 Trade Review (Automatic)
[L:414] +After every close, the system generates:
[L:415] +- **Thesis vs Reality**: Did the setup play out as expected?
[L:416] +- **Entry Quality**: Was entry at the optimal zone? Did price retrace deeper?
[L:417] +- **Risk Quality**: Was stop loss placed correctly? Was it too tight or too loose?
[L:418] +- **Exit Quality**: Were targets hit? Was trailing stop optimal?
[L:419] +- **Market Context**: What was the regime? Did it change during the trade?
[L:420] +- **Outcome Classification**:
[L:421] +  - Correct thesis, good execution, profit
[L:422] +  - Correct thesis, poor execution, loss (moved stop, wrong size)
[L:423] +  - Incorrect thesis, good risk management, small loss
[L:424] +  - Incorrect thesis, poor risk management, large loss
[L:425] +  - Data failure (bad data caused bad decision)
[L:426] +  - Model failure (ML prediction was wrong)
[L:427] +  - Strategy mismatch (strategy did not fit regime)
