[L:431] +## 8. The Learning System — Controlled Improvement
[L:432] +
[L:433] +### 8.1 The Learning Loop
[L:434] +
[L:435] +```
[L:436] +Trade Completed
[L:437] +    ↓
[L:438] +Trade Review Generated
[L:439] +    ↓
[L:440] +Pattern Recognition: "This setup has occurred 12 times before"
[L:441] +    ↓
[L:442] +Historical Outcome: "8 wins, 4 losses, 66% win rate, 1.8 profit factor"
[L:443] +    ↓
[L:444] +Hypothesis: "This setup works better in London session than NY session"
[L:445] +    ↓
[L:446] +Experiment: Track London vs NY performance for 20 more occurrences
[L:447] +    ↓
[L:448] +Validation: Statistical significance reached
[L:449] +    ↓
[L:450] +Knowledge Update: "BOS + Sweep + OB setup: London win rate 75%, NY win rate 50%"
[L:451] +    ↓
[L:452] +Strategy Adjustment: Reduce size for NY session, increase for London
[L:453] +    ↓
[L:454] +Versioned Knowledge stored in Knowledge Graph
[L:455] +```
[L:456] +
[L:457] +### 8.2 Knowledge Graph
[L:458] +
[L:459] +The system maintains a graph of validated knowledge:
[L:460] +
[L:461] +```
[L:462] +[Setup: BOS + Sweep + OB] → performs_well_in → [Regime: Trending]
[L:463] +[Setup: BOS + Sweep + OB] → performs_poorly_in → [Session: Asian]
[L:464] +[Pattern: Bullish Engulfing] → confirms → [Setup: OB Mitigation]
[L:465] +[Indicator: RSI < 30] → supports → [Setup: Mean Reversion]
[L:466] +[Lesson: "Moving stop loss increases average loss by 40%"] → learned_from → [Trade: #1247]
[L:467] +```
[L:468] +
[L:469] +### 8.3 No Uncontrolled Self-Modification
[L:470] +
[L:471] +The system **never** automatically changes:
[L:472] +- Stop loss rules
[L:473] +- Position sizing rules
[L:474] +- Risk limits
[L:475] +- Strategy logic
[L:476] +- Model weights
[L:477] +
[L:478] +It produces **recommendations** that must be reviewed and approved by the user (or a research workflow) before being promoted to production.
