[L:621] +## 13. Technology Stack — What I Would Actually Use
[L:622] +
[L:623] +### 13.1 Frontend
[L:624] +- **React 18 + TypeScript 5.5** — Keep the existing foundation. It works.
[L:625] +- **Vite 5** — Fast builds, hot reload. Keep it.
[L:626] +- **Tailwind CSS 3** — Utility-first, rapid UI development.
[L:627] +- **Lightweight Charts** — For candlestick charts. Fast, clean, no bloat.
[L:628] +- **Custom Canvas Overlay** — For drawing structure, liquidity, OBs, FVGs. Lightweight Charts doesn't support complex annotations natively, so I would build a Canvas overlay layer on top of it.
[L:629] +- **Zustand** — Minimal state. UI state only.
[L:630] +- **TanStack Query** — Server state, caching, background refetch.
[L:631] +- **React Router 6** — Client-side routing.
[L:632] +- **Lucide React** — Icons.
[L:633] +
[L:634] +### 13.2 Backend
[L:635] +- **Node.js 20 + Fastify** — The API layer. Fastify is faster than Express, has built-in validation, and excellent WebSocket support. TypeScript is the right choice for trading logic — financial math in Python is fine, but orchestration and state management are better in TypeScript.
[L:636] +- **Supabase PostgreSQL** — Database. Keep it. Add migrations for the full schema.
[L:637] +- **Supabase Auth** — Authentication. Keep it.
[L:638] +- **Redis** — Hot cache for latest candles, active decisions, session state, rate limiting.
[L:639] +- **Deno Edge Functions (Supabase)** — Only for auth hooks and lightweight data transforms. NOT for ML, NOT for backtesting, NOT for real-time streaming.
[L:640] +
[L:641] +### 13.3 Machine Learning
[L:642] +- **TensorFlow.js** — Client-side inference only. Lightweight pre-trained models.
[L:643] +- **Server-side ML** — If needed, a separate TypeScript/Deno service (not Python, per the Master Prompt). But honestly, for MVP, I would skip deep learning entirely and use:
[L:644] +  - **LightGBM via ONNX runtime** — If we can export a LightGBM model to ONNX and run it in Node.js
[L:645] +  - **Or simple statistical models** — Logistic regression ensemble, already in the existing codebase
[L:646] +- **MLflow-style registry** — Simple versioned model storage in PostgreSQL
[L:647] +
[L:648] +### 13.4 Market Data
[L:649] +- **EODHD REST API** — Historical data, daily backfill
[L:650] +- **EODHD WebSocket** — Real-time streams
[L:651] +- **Provider abstraction** — `MarketDataProvider` interface. EODHD is the primary. Binance can be secondary for crypto-specific data.
[L:652] +
[L:653] +### 13.5 Real-Time
[L:654] +- **WebSocket server (Node.js + ws library)** — Dedicated service for pushing candles, decisions, and drawings to the frontend.
[L:655] +- **Server-Sent Events (SSE)** — For decision updates and alerts (simpler than WebSockets for one-way push).
