[L:1] +# Quantum — Chief Engineer Build Specification
[L:2] +## Opinionated Architecture for an Evidence-Based Trading Intelligence Platform
[L:3] +
[L:4] +---
[L:5] +
[L:6] +## 1. Executive Vision
[L:7] +
[L:8] +Quantum is an **event-driven, multi-engine quantitative trading intelligence platform**. It is not a dashboard with indicators. It is a **decision system** that ingests market data, runs parallel analytical engines, synthesizes weighted evidence, applies risk gates, and produces auditable trade decisions for paper trading.
[L:9] +
[L:10] +### Core Architectural Principles
[L:11] +
[L:12] +1. **Event-Driven, Not Request-Driven** — The system reacts to market events (new candles), not user clicks. This makes backtesting, real-time analysis, and paper trading the same pipeline.
[L:13] +2. **Engine Plugin Architecture** — Every analytical domain is a self-contained plugin. Add a new engine without touching the decision core.
[L:14] +3. **Server-Side Intelligence, Client-Side Presentation** — All computation, ML, and backtesting happen on the server. The frontend is a thin, reactive shell.
[L:15] +4. **Point-in-Time Correctness** — Every feature, pattern, and decision is computable only with data available at that exact moment. Look-ahead bias is architecturally impossible.
[L:16] +5. **Explainability by Contract** — No engine can emit a signal without a human-readable explanation. This is enforced at the type level.
[L:17] +
[L:18] +---
[L:19] +
[L:20] +## 2. Technology Stack (With Justification)
[L:21] +
[L:22] +### Frontend
[L:23] +- **Next.js 14 (App Router)** — Server Components for data-heavy dashboards, streaming SSR for decision panels, API Routes for proxying secrets. React 18 + Vite is fine for SPAs; Next.js is the right choice for a data platform.
[L:24] +- **TypeScript 5.5** — Strict mode, no exceptions.
[L:25] +- **Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui** — Rapid UI development with accessible, composable primitives.
[L:26] +- **Zustand** — Minimal global state. Only UI state (sidebar, theme, alerts). No server state here.
[L:27] +- **TanStack Query v5** — Server state, caching, background refetching. The frontend does not own data; it subscribes to it.
[L:28] +- **Lightweight Charts** — Financial charting. Fast, canvas-based, no dependencies.
[L:29] +- **tRPC** — End-to-end typesafe API calls from Next.js to the API service. No REST contract drift.
[L:30] +
[L:31] +### Backend Services
[L:32] +- **Node.js 20 + Fastify** — The trading API and orchestration layer. Fastify is faster than Express, has built-in schema validation, and excellent WebSocket support.
[L:33] +- **Python 3.11 + FastAPI** — ML service only. Feature engineering, model training, inference. Kept separate because Python is non-negotiable for ML, but TypeScript is better for trading logic.
[L:34] +- **Deno Edge Functions (Supabase)** — Only for auth hooks, simple CRUD, and lightweight data transformations. Not for ML, not for backtesting, not for real-time streaming.
[L:35] +
[L:36] +### Data & Messaging
[L:37] +- **PostgreSQL 15 (Supabase)** — User data, decisions, positions, backtest metadata. Row Level Security enforced.
[L:38] +- **TimescaleDB** — Time-series extension for PostgreSQL. Stores OHLCV candles, feature vectors, and historical evidence. Native compression, continuous aggregates, time-based partitioning.
[L:39] +- **Redis 7** — Hot cache for latest candles, active decisions, session state, rate limiting, and pub/sub for real-time events.
[L:40] +- **Apache Kafka (or Redpanda)** — Event bus. Decouples market data ingestion from analysis engines from decision engine from paper trading. Every service publishes and consumes events. This is the backbone.
[L:41] +
[L:42] +### Machine Learning
[L:43] +- **LightGBM** — Primary model. Gradient boosting on tabular features. Fast to train, interpretable, and hard to beat on structured data.
[L:44] +- **PyTorch** — Only for sequence models (LSTM) if LightGBM proves profitable first.
[L:45] +- **MLflow** — Model registry, experiment tracking, artifact storage.
[L:46] +- **Feast** — Feature store. Point-in-time correct feature retrieval. This is non-negotiable for trading ML.
[L:47] +
[L:48] +### Infrastructure
[L:49] +- **Docker + Docker Compose** — Local development.
[L:50] +- **Kubernetes (or Railway/Render for MVP)** — Production orchestration.
[L:51] +- **GitHub Actions** — CI/CD.
[L:52] +- **Turborepo + pnpm** — Monorepo management.
[L:53] +
[L:54] +---
[L:55] +
