[L:1200] +
[L:1201] +## 16. Security Architecture
[L:1202] +
[L:1203] +### Authentication
[L:1204] +- Supabase Auth with email/password
[L:1205] +- JWT tokens, refreshed automatically
[L:1206] +- Protected tRPC procedures verify JWT on every request
[L:1207] +
[L:1208] +### Authorization
[L:1209] +- Row Level Security on all PostgreSQL tables
[L:1210] +- User can only access their own data
[L:1211] +- API validates `user_id` matches authenticated user
[L:1212] +
[L:1213] +### Secrets Management
[L:1214] +- API keys (EODHD, etc.) stored in environment variables, never in code
[L:1215] +- Frontend never sees API keys — all external API calls proxy through Next.js API routes or the API service
[L:1216] +- ML service API key shared only between API service and ML service
[L:1217] +
[L:1218] +### Input Validation
[L:1219] +- Zod schemas on all tRPC inputs
[L:1220] +- Fastify schema validation on all HTTP endpoints
[L:1221] +- SQL injection impossible via parameterized queries (Prisma or Drizzle)
[L:1222] +
[L:1223] +### Rate Limiting
[L:1224] +- Redis-based rate limiting on API
[L:1225] +- Market data ingestion rate-limited per provider
[L:1226] +- WebSocket connection limits per user
[L:1227] +
