[L:107] +
[L:108] +## 2. Technology Stack (With Justification)
[L:109] +
[L:110] +### 2.1 Frontend
[L:111] +- **React 18** — Component model, ecosystem, team familiarity.
[L:112] +- **TypeScript 5.5** — Strict mode. Zero `any` types in trading logic.
[L:113] +- **Vite 5** — Fast HMR, native ESM, simpler config than webpack.
[L:114] +- **Tailwind CSS 3** — Utility-first, rapid UI iteration, dark mode support.
[L:115] +- **Lightweight Charts** — Financial charting. 60fps, no dependencies, perfect for candlesticks.
[L:116] +- **Custom HTML5 Canvas Overlay** — Sits on top of Lightweight Charts. Draws structure, liquidity, OBs, FVGs, entry zones, SL, targets. Full control over rendering.
[L:117] +- **Zustand** — UI state only (sidebar, theme, chart settings, alert visibility). No server state.
[L:118] +- **TanStack Query v5** — Server state, caching, background refetch, optimistic updates.
[L:119] +- **React Router 6** — Client-side routing, protected routes by role.
[L:120] +- **Lucide React** — Consistent iconography.
[L:121] +- **Recharts / Visx** — For dashboard metrics, equity curves, pie charts (not for candlesticks).
[L:122] +
[L:123] +### 2.2 Backend
[L:124] +- **Node.js 20 LTS** — Runtime.
[L:125] +- **Fastify 4** — Faster than Express, built-in JSON schema validation, excellent plugin architecture, native WebSocket support.
[L:126] +- **TypeScript 5.5** — Same language as frontend. Shared types package.
[L:127] +- **Prisma ORM** — Type-safe database access, migration management, query optimization.
[L:128] +- **Zod** — Runtime schema validation for all API inputs.
[L:129] +- **JWT (jsonwebtoken)** — Auth tokens, role claims.
[L:130] +- **bcrypt** — Password hashing.
[L:131] +- **Helmet** — Security headers.
[L:132] +- **Rate-limiter-flexible** — Redis-backed rate limiting.
[L:133] +
[L:134] +### 2.3 Data & Messaging
[L:135] +- **Supabase PostgreSQL 15** — Primary database. Auth, user data, decisions, positions, backtests.
[L:136] +- **TimescaleDB Extension** — For candle storage. Native compression, continuous aggregates, time-based partitioning. Critical for 5+ years of 1m data.
[L:137] +- **Redis 7** — Hot cache (latest candles, active decisions, sessions), rate limiting, pub/sub for real-time events.
[L:138] +- **Supabase Auth** — Email/password auth, JWT sessions, RLS integration.
[L:139] +
[L:140] +### 2.4 Machine Learning
[L:141] +- **ONNX Runtime Node.js** — Run exported LightGBM/XGBoost models in Node.js. No Python required.
[L:142] +- **TensorFlow.js** — Client-side inference only (pre-trained lightweight models). No training in browser.
[L:143] +- **Simple Statistics / MLJS** — TypeScript statistical libraries for baseline models (logistic regression, k-means for regimes).
[L:144] +- **Custom Feature Pipeline** — TypeScript feature engineering, point-in-time correct.
[L:145] +
[L:146] +### 2.5 DevOps
[L:147] +- **Docker + Docker Compose** — Local development stack.
[L:148] +- **Turborepo + pnpm** — Monorepo management, task pipelining, caching.
[L:149] +- **GitHub Actions** — CI/CD: typecheck, lint, test, build, deploy.
[L:150] +- **Vercel** — Frontend hosting.
[L:151] +- **Railway / Render** — Backend services (API, WS, Ingest, ML).
[L:152] +- **Supabase** — Managed PostgreSQL + Auth.
[L:153] +- **Upstash** — Managed Redis.
[L:154] +
