[L:439] +## 4. UI/UX Design Specification
[L:440] +
[L:441] +### 4.1 Design Philosophy
[L:442] +- **Dark mode default** — Traders operate in low-light environments. Dark reduces eye strain.
[L:443] +- **Information density** — Professional terminals show maximum relevant data. No wasted space.
[L:444] +- **Color semantics** — Green = bullish/profit/approved. Red = bearish/loss/rejected. Yellow = warning/watch. Blue = structure/information. Orange = order blocks. Purple = breaker blocks. Cyan = FVGs.
[L:445] +- **Motion** — Subtle animations for state changes (decision bar slide-in, evidence meter fill, alert pulse). No distracting motion.
[L:446] +- **Accessibility** — All drawings must have ARIA labels. Color is not the only indicator (patterns, labels, icons).
[L:447] +
