[L:1143] +---
[L:1144] +
[L:1145] +## 9. Key Architectural Decisions
[L:1146] +
[L:1147] +### 9.1 Why Fastify over Express?
[L:1148] +- 2x faster request handling
[L:1149] +- Built-in JSON schema validation (Zod integration)
[L:1150] +- Native async/await support
[L:1151] +- Excellent plugin architecture for auth, RBAC, rate limiting
[L:1152] +- Better WebSocket support
[L:1153] +
[L:1154] +### 9.2 Why Custom Canvas Overlay instead of TradingView Charting Library?
[L:1155] +- TradingView Library is heavy (MBs of JS), proprietary, and licensing is complex
[L:1156] +- Lightweight Charts + Canvas overlay gives us full control over drawing logic
[L:1157] +- We can render ICT/SMC-specific drawings (OBs, FVGs, liquidity sweeps) that TradingView doesn't natively support
[L:1158] +- Performance is better — we only render what we need
[L:1159] +- No external dependency on TradingView's rendering engine
[L:1160] +
[L:1161] +### 9.3 Why TimescaleDB over standard PostgreSQL for candles?
[L:1162] +- 90% compression on OHLCV data
[L:1163] +- Automatic time-based partitioning (hypertables)
[L:1164] +- Continuous aggregates for pre-computed indicators
[L:1165] +- Querying 5 years of 1m candles is fast without manual sharding
[L:1166] +- It's a PostgreSQL extension — no separate database to manage
[L:1167] +
[L:1168] +### 9.4 Why ONNX Runtime instead of Python for ML?
[L:1169] +- Master Prompt explicitly discourages Python unless justified
[L:1170] +- LightGBM models can be exported to ONNX and run in Node.js
[L:1171] +- Latency is comparable (< 10ms difference)
[L:1172] +- No separate Python service to deploy, monitor, and secure
[L:1173] +- Same TypeScript types shared between feature engineering and inference
[L:1174] +
[L:1175] +### 9.5 Why Redis Pub/Sub instead of Kafka for real-time?
[L:1176] +- Kafka is overkill for MVP-scale real-time (we're pushing to maybe 100 concurrent users)
[L:1177] +- Redis Pub/Sub is simpler, lower latency, and already required for caching
[L:1178] +- Can migrate to Kafka later if we need persistence, replay, or consumer groups
[L:1179] +- Current event volume: ~1 event per second per symbol. Redis handles 100k+ messages/sec.
[L:1180] +
[L:1181] +### 9.6 Why three roles instead of two?
[L:1182] +- **User**: Trades, views own data. Cannot break others.
[L:1183] +- **Admin**: Manages community strategies, views analytics. Cannot break infrastructure.
[L:1184] +- **Super Admin**: Infrastructure control. Can emergency stop. Separation of concerns prevents accidents.
[L:1185] +
